# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 13 — Search, Filtering, Sorting & Export

---

# Purpose

This section defines everything users can search, filter, sort, and export in DigiSwasthya.

If a dataset is visible in the product, its findability rules belong here.

---

# Principles

1. Users can only search/filter/export what they can View.
2. Default sorts must match operational urgency where applicable.
3. Filters are conjunctive unless stated otherwise.
4. Search is practical business search, not unconstrained global data mining across businesses.
5. Exports honour the same permissions and current filters.
6. Empty results are valid outcomes, not errors.

---

# Global Search Behaviour

## Query Basics

- Trim whitespace
- Case-insensitive for text codes/names
- Partial match on names/codes where useful
- Exact match preferred for IDs, GST, phone, invoice numbers

## Empty Query

- Show default list with default sort and no search constraint

## No Result

- Show empty state; retain filters so user can adjust

